30-Second Interview Summary
We deploy Spring Boot microservices as Docker containers in Kubernetes Deployments. Services provide stable access, Ingress handles routing, ConfigMaps and Secrets externalize configuration, Actuator endpoints support readiness/liveness probes, HPA enables auto-scaling, and Rolling Updates provide zero-downtime deployments. On AWS EKS, images are stored in ECR and deployed via Kubernetes manifests or Helm charts.
